<title>SPAIN: Employer, union take break in Spain labour talks.</title>
<headline>Employer, union take break in Spain labour talks.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish employers and unions took a break on Tuesday in key labour reform talks and will resume at 1530 GMT, a spokesman for workers' commission union CCOO said.</p>
<p>&quot;The two sides are breaking for lunch and will resume talks at 1530 GMT,&quot; said a spokesman for CCOO.</p>
<p>The two sides are trying to reach a deal on labour reform before the government steps in and imposes a deal.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
